# Tests of the assembler that do not pass, and why.  run-suite.sh reads
# this: a test named here is expected to fail, and the suite fails if it
# passes, so the line goes in the commit that mends the cause.
#
# name <white space> reason.  Every one is a defect of the assembler but
# those marked SKIP; AS-T-nnn is the task in docs/as-tasks.md that mends
# it.  A reason beginning SKIP means the test is not run: these build
# inside the source tree and `make clean` it.
#
# Each line was checked by running the test with GNU as in this
# assembler's place: a test GNU passes fails here for a fault of this
# assembler's.  Where GNU failed too, its failure was read.  Three tests
# asked for what GNU does not do and were corrected (an %ss: prefix GNU
# omits, in the two i8086 tests; Intel's lodsd and stosd in AT&T source,
# in test_intel_dual_syntax); the rest fail with GNU only where they ask
# for this assembler's own messages and options, past the fault listed.
#
# Tests whose expectation was stale -- the assembler having since changed
# on purpose -- were corrected rather than listed: test_directive_surface
# (.if and .macro exist), test_x86_64_short_local_temp_branch and
# test_x86_local_temp_branch_runtime (a branch within a section is
# resolved, not relocated), test_lexer_core (string tokens are raw),
# test_output_binary (code is padded with NOPs), test_testing_fuzz_perf
# (the object is the assembler's own, not GNU's byte for byte).
test_build_matrix.sh	SKIP builds with NATIVE_BUILD=1 in usr.bin/as and asserts the Makefile's text of April; to be rewritten (AS-T-013)
test_integration_matrix.sh	SKIP builds with NATIVE_BUILD=1 in usr.bin/as (AS-T-013)
test_integration_rollout.sh	SKIP runs make clean in usr.bin/as and builds there twice (AS-T-013)
test_cli_defsym.sh	--defsym is taken and never read: the name stays undefined (AS-T-139)
test_cli_warnings.sh	--no-warn and -W silence nothing and --fatal-warnings fails nothing (AS-T-142, AS-T-145); a warning is written four times (AS-T-392)
test_complex_control_32_64.sh	a ; inside a comment begins a statement: gcc -fverbose-asm writes "# for (i = 0; i < 32; i++)" (AS-T-093)
test_diagnostics_determinism.sh	a message names the temporary file and its line, not the user's (AS-T-090, AS-T-147)
test_fuzz_matrix.sh	runs test_testing_fuzz_perf.sh
test_i386_encoding.sh	`add %eax, %xmm0` is assembled: a register's class is not checked (AS-T-171)
test_i8086_corpus.sh	16-bit code: refused at a line with an empty message (AS-T-347, AS-T-147)
test_i8086_elf_object.sh	16-bit code, as above (AS-T-347)
test_i8086_realmode_core.sh	16-bit code, as above (AS-T-347)
test_isa_heavy_64.sh	vmovdqu is not a mnemonic (AS-T-332)
test_output_binary.sh	code is padded with one-byte NOPs, not GNU's sequences (AS-T-251)
test_relocations_elf_32_64.sh	a forced short jump out of range is assembled and should be refused (AS-T-221)
test_sections_symbols_expr_32_64.sh	--64: "failed to emit relocations" for a data relocation narrower than 64 bits (AS-T-210)
test_source_model_32_64.sh	the first error ends the run: a source with three bad lines gets one message, where GNU gives three (AS-T-388)
test_testing_fuzz_perf.sh	runs test_relocations_elf_32_64.sh
test_unit_matrix.sh	runs test_i8086_corpus.sh
test_x86_32_corpus_intel_roundtrip.sh	the corpus is not one GNU as passes, and this assembler stops where GNU first does: line 1809, `bnd callw` (GNU: "bnd is not supported on i386"); GNU refuses line 2817 as well, wrgsbase in 32-bit code.  The corpus wants mending before the test says anything of the assembler
test_x86_64_corpus_intel_roundtrip.sh	`rep nop`, which is pause, is refused (AS-T-031).  Past that the test is not yet one GNU as passes: GNU refuses lines of the Intel source it generates (a suffix on jg)
test_x86_64_encoding.sh	jrcxz to a label is refused with the message "?" (AS-T-037)
test_x86_avx512f_core.sh	EVEX vaddpd is encoded with W = 0 (AS-T-339)
test_x86_avx_core.sh	vpermilps is not encoded (AS-T-327)
